                        "review": "Wish i could give this a thumbs up, but looking past the superficial issues there is a problem at the core of the game which prevents it from getting a recommendation here\n\n[h1]Rating[/h1]\nTactic fans looking for a fix: 75%\neveryone else: 50%\n\n[h1]Content[/h1]\n+ at the time of writing this im about 34h in and there is still a couple story missions left (+3x side missions if you want to do those)\n- the missions have become an absolute drag, 7 of my ships vs 30+ enemy ships has become the standard, its not actually difficult (see AI) just takes forever for the AI to move and for you to clean up that many ships\n- story is 100% linear so far with mostly battles and once in a while a multiple choice random event where you have to guess the right answer\n- all missions feel the same \n+ plenty of ships / research / items / crew\n- more than half the stuff is useless and a good portion of the rest you will not experience because researching upgrades for more than 3-4 ships is not feasible due to limited data (research resource), item research is especially bad since you first have to research it and then still pay for buying items\n\n[h1]Polish[/h1]\n+ game is stable (hasnt crashed at all for me) and i havnt encountered any game breaking bugs ([strike]there seemes to be atleast one with a certain upgrade, which is being addressed[/strike] (fixed))\n- vital information missing from the UI\n* what abilities do ships have before you buy them\n* which ship classes some of the hero ships actually belong to\n* how does initiative work (i have ships with 65 that are sometimes at the top of the queue and next turn at the bottom)\n* it says on the mission screen \"Optional deployments normally recharge after every successful story mission\", except when they dont and a recruitment side mission pops up and you are out of deployments\n[strike]- minor issues with some side missions, where you cant complete those, just reload and pick a different one[/strike] (fixed)\n[strike]- in alot of missions (especially towards the end) story dialog is not playing at all, with a linear story this is a major oversight during testing[/strike] (fixed)\n\n[h1]AI / Difficulty[/h1] (based on middle difficulty and im not going to start over again just too much drag):\n- basically non existent\n* AI will shot at different ships randomly instead of focus fire\n* AI will shot at ships behind cover instead of popping in and out of cover\n* AI carriers will run away from fighters placed next to them, in general moving next to AI ships will make those move away and then shot you with cover blocking them\n* AI will shot at ships with abysmal rates of actually hitting those (i had ships being shot at 15 times per round and get hit once) and will not use missiles / AoE attacks unless it can hit multiple ships\n- dodge > everything else (my smugglers with 64/44 tank far better than my flagship with 114/146), which means less firepower on your side (more drag) but if they cant kill you at all you win by default\n\n[h1]Communication[/h1]\n+ active in the forums and working on fixes\n\nAs a fan of tactical games i can look past some of the minor issues and i dont regret buying the game. However at the core the game is defined by boring and brainless cookie cutter missions that is best dealt with in small increments of playing it.",
